{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1695,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Columbus lied to his own crew about how far they'd sailed. It still almost wasn't enough.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 117
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "September, fourteen ninety-two. Three small ships sail west from the Canary Islands.",
   "from": 121,
   "to": 236
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, Columbus keeps two counts of distance: a true one, and a shorter one for the crew, so they won't panic.",
   "from": 251,
   "to": 402
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Weeks pass. No land.",
   "from": 406,
   "to": 444
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "October tenth. The crew has had enough.",
   "from": 448,
   "to": 509
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "sailor",
   "text": "Admiral, turn back!",
   "from": 513,
   "to": 545
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "His log, known only from a friar's summary, says he calmed them. Some later writers say he made a deal: three more days.",
   "from": 548,
   "to": 728
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Next day, the sea sends clues. A carved stick. A branch with berries.",
   "from": 731,
   "to": 842
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "sailor",
   "text": "Look! Someone carved this!",
   "from": 846,
   "to": 896
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Two in the morning, October twelfth, a lookout shouts.",
   "from": 899,
   "to": 965
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "lookout",
   "text": "Land! Land!",
   "from": 968,
   "to": 1017
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Now, what if they had turned back? Someone else would almost certainly have crossed. Portugal reached Brazil in fifteen hundred.",
   "from": 1021,
   "to": 1164
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But this crossing started the great swap. Potatoes and chocolate went east. Smallpox went west, and with war and slavery, killed most of the Americas' native people.",
   "from": 1168,
   "to": 1435
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "A lie, one tense night, and a few twigs. That's how close they came to turning around.",
   "from": 1439,
   "to": 1582
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And the lookout's reward? Columbus said he'd seen a light first, and kept it.",
   "from": 1586,
   "to": 1671
  }
 ],
